{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":10983,"ns":0,"title":"First-order logic","extract":"In mathematics, philosophy, linguistics, and computer science, first-order logic (FOL), also called predicate logic, predicate calculus, or quantificational logic, is a type of formal system. First-order logic uses quantified variables over non-logical objects, and allows the use of sentences that contain variables.","description":"Type of logical system","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}